SHEPHERD = {
"claim":"The sheep want to hear the shepherd's voice.",
"body":[
"In John 10, Jesus says the sheep listen to his voice, he calls his own by name, and they follow him because they know his voice. He says it three different ways in eight verses, which is what a writer does when he wants to make sure you do not miss it.",
"That is the argument for the pastor shooting these himself, and it is worth making to him plainly, because most pastors will try to hand this off.",
"A polished devotional read by a professional is a better product and a worse pastoral act. The person watching on Tuesday morning is not evaluating production. They are checking whether the man who preached on Sunday actually meant it on a weekday, in his kitchen, in a shirt he has worn before.",
"Ninety seconds. Shot on the phone in his pocket. One story in each one, because a teaching without a story is a memo and nobody watches a memo twice.",
"The mistake is trying to make it good. It does not need to be good. It needs to be him.",
],
}

